{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Ho, drunkards of Ephraim.</b> For the princes were occupied with wine." "<b>Tsvi.</b> Like 'for beauty and for glory' (Isaiah 4:2)." "The meaning of <b>ateret</b> concerns kingship." "<b>Head of the valley of fats.</b> 'Head' like 'chief spices' (Song of Songs 4:14), and they were so numerous that it reverted like 'valley,' like 'and we dwelt in the valley' (Deuteronomy 3:29). And some say like 'valley, greatly' (Isaiah 16:9), which is missing a he." "<b>Clots of.</b> Like 'they struck me, I knew not' (Proverbs 23:35)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:29.824384873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}